## 1.3 Mandatory implementation rules

1. Inspect the existing GovAI Nexus repository before development.
2. Reuse the existing authentication, database and API architecture.
3. Reuse existing application, department, service, scheme, employee and officer records.
4. Do not create duplicate master data.
5. Do not replace the existing backend with Node.js.
6. Use Python FastAPI for all AI and analytics APIs.
7. All charts must use real authorized data or clearly identified sample/demo data.
8. Never display fabricated government statistics.
9. Never invent model accuracy, prediction scores or evaluation metrics.
10. Implement loading, empty, error and insufficient-data states.
11. Enforce role and jurisdiction permissions on the backend.
12. Maintain source references for AI-generated government information.
13. Do not automatically make legally significant government decisions using AI.
14. Do not treat an anomaly alert as proof of fraud.
15. Do not publish confidential citizen records in public dashboards.

