- Page heading and description at the top.
- Filters aligned on the right when space permits.
- KPI cards directly below the page heading.
- Charts and tables in responsive grid layouts.

## 17.2 Standard page structure

Every analytics page must follow this hierarchy:

1. Breadcrumb.
2. Page title.
3. Page description.
4. Reporting period and refresh status.
5. Global filters.
6. KPI cards.
7. Primary charts.
8. Detailed analytics.
9. Data tables.
10. Insights and recommendations.
11. Export / reporting actions.

Do not force identical layouts on every page. Preserve the shared hierarchy while arranging charts and tables according to the page's purpose.

## 17.3 KPI card alignment

- Use 4 cards per row on wide desktop layouts where space permits.
- Use 3 cards per row on medium desktop layouts.
- Use 2 cards per row on tablets.
- Use 1 or 2 cards per row on mobile depending on readability.

All KPI cards in the same row must have consistent heights.

Use consistent icon positioning, label spacing and number typography.

## 17.4 Chart alignment

Use:

- Two-column chart layouts for major comparisons.
- Full-width charts for detailed trends.
- Consistent chart heights within the same row.
- Proper axis labels.
- Readable legends.
- Tooltips.
- Date filters.
- Responsive chart containers.

Do not overcrowd charts with unnecessary metrics.

## 17.5 Table alignment

All tables must have:

- Consistent header height.
- Proper column alignment.
- Readable spacing.
- Search.
- Filters.
- Pagination.
- Sorting.
- Empty state.
- Loading state.
- Error state.
- Responsive overflow handling.

Use right alignment for numerical metrics where appropriate.

Use clear status badges.

## 17.6 Colour alignment

Maintain consistent meanings:

- Navy: Main navigation and primary brand.
- Purple: Active module and AI intelligence.
- Blue: General analytics.
- Teal / Green: Healthy or positive state.
- Amber: Warning.
- Red: Critical issue.
- Grey: Inactive or unknown.

Do not use colours as the only way to convey status.

## 17.7 Mobile responsiveness

At mobile widths:

- Collapse sidebar into a drawer.
- Keep page titles readable.
- Stack KPI cards.
- Convert chart grids into one-column layouts.
- Make filters accessible.
- Make tables horizontally scrollable or convert them into record cards.
- Keep critical alert information visible.
- Avoid horizontal page overflow.

## 17.8 Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA.

Implement:

- Keyboard navigation.
- Visible focus.
- Accessible form labels.
- Sufficient contrast.
- Chart descriptions.
- Screen-reader support.
- Tamil text support.
- Accessible modal dialogs.

